The difference between MC2 and MC3 isn't that great.  I think MC2 works
75% of the time while MC3 works 99% of the time.  You can definitely go
through the game with MC2 if you want to.

Protection isn't that great.  An extra 3 AC points is nice, but
displacement actually causes monsters to miss you, cast spells in the
wrong direction, and zap wands at the wrong spot.  AC can't do that.
And if a monster guesses where you are just move and they have to guess
your new location.

As you can guess I like displacement.  I vividly remember a game where
I was in Minetown with a pet large dog ... I was a low level priestess
with a CoD.  A group of ogres generated and one killed my dog.  The
other two attacked me but kept missing because of displacement.
Eventually I was able to kill all 3 with hardly any hit points left.
If I'd had a CoP instead, I would have certainly died.

Finally, I'm not sure why anyone would not want to be permanently
invisible.  It's useful and you can put on a mummy wrapping if you want
to shop.



